window.docContents[51].resolve({"/part-5-applications/ch18-completion/#ch18-completion":{"contents":"\n\nIn Chapter 5 we saw \\mathbb{L} / \\mathbb{I} \\simeq \\mathbb{R}, and starting from hyperrationals \\mathbb{Q}^* instead of \\mathbb{R}^* constructs \\mathbb{R} \\simeq \\mathbb{Q}^*_{\\mathrm{fin}} / \\mathbb{Q}^*_{\\mathrm{inf}} without ever mentioning Cauchy equivalence classes or Dedekind cuts! In Ch18_Completion.lean (5,078 lines), we execute this universal Nonstandard Hull recipe across four settings:\n\n* Metric & Banach Nonstandard Hulls: For any metric or normed space M in an \\aleph_1-saturated enlargement, let M_{\\mathrm{fin}} = \\{x \\in {}^*M : {}^*d(x, {}^*x_0) \\in \\mathbb{L}\\} and identify x \\approx y \\iff {}^*d(x, y) \\in \\mathbb{I}. Countable saturation guarantees that the quotient \\widehat{M} = M_{\\mathrm{fin}} / {\\approx} with distance \\hat{d}([x], [y]) = \\mathrm{sh}({}^*d(x, y)) is automatically Cauchy complete (a complete metric space / Banach space into which M embeds isometrically as a dense subspace)!* p-adic Integers \\mathbb{Z}_p & Field \\mathbb{Q}_p: Equipping \\mathbb{Z} and \\mathbb{Q} with the p-adic valuation |x|_p = p^{-\\mathrm{ord}_p(x)}, two hyperintegers z, w \\in {}^*\\mathbb{Z} are p-adically infinitesimally close iff p^n \\mid (z - w) for every standard n \\in \\mathbb{N}. Quotienting {}^*\\mathbb{Z} by \\bigcap_{n \\in \\mathbb{N}} p^n\\,{}^*\\mathbb{Z} produces \\mathbb{Z}_p, where every p-adic integer is represented literally by the base-p digits of a single hypernatural!* Formal Power Series R⟦X⟧: Quotienting hyperpolynomials of unlimited degree modulo (X^\\omega) recovers formal power series via finite-degree truncations.\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt.Ch18\n\n#check @hyperratQuotient_isField\n#check @padicInfClose_hypernat_iff_eq_basePDigits\n#check @exists_pos_hypernat_baseP_expansion_of_padicInt\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part V — Landmark Applications & Reading Guide","header":"5.3. Chapter 18: Completion by Enlargement — Hulls,  <missing> -adics & Power Series","id":"/part-5-applications/ch18-completion/#ch18-completion"}});